{"abstract":"This notice requests information from the public about potential regulatory changes that may reduce regulatory burdens and promote access to mortgage credit, as appropriate and consistent with applicable law. The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (Bureau or CFPB) seeks to reduce unwarranted regulatory burdens to ensure that creditworthy borrowers can access mortgage credit. Specifically, the CFPB is requesting information on industry and consumer burdens related to the integrated mortgage disclosures under the Truth in Lending Act (TILA) and Real Estate Settlement Procedures Act (RESPA) (TILA-RESPA integrated disclosures or TRID), the right of rescission, and reverse mortgage disclosures.","action":"Notice; request for information.","agencies":[{"raw_name":"Consumer Financial Protection Bureau","name":"Consumer Financial Protection Bureau","id":573,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/consumer-financial-protection-bureau","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/573","parent_id":null,"slug":"consumer-financial-protection-bureau"}],"body_html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/html/2026/07/09/2026-13834.html","cfr_references":[{"chapter":null,"citation_url":null,"part":"1024","title":12},{"chapter":null,"citation_url":null,"part":"1026","title":12}],"citation":"91 FR 42382","comment_url":null,"comments_close_on":"2026-08-10","correction_of":null,"corrections":[],"dates":"Comments must be received on or before August 10, 2026.","disposition_notes":null,"docket_ids":["Docket No. CFPB-2026-0018"],"dockets":[{"supporting_documents":[],"agency_name":"CFPB","documents":[{"comment_count":341,"comment_start_date":"2026-07-09","updated_at":"2026-09-09T01:56:21.917-04:00","comment_url":"https://www.regulations.gov/commenton/CFPB-2026-0018-0001","allow_late_comments":false,"id":"CFPB-2026-0018-0001","comment_end_date":"2026-08-11","regulations_dot_gov_open_for_comment":false}],"supporting_documents_count":0,"i